{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Unsupervised Feature Relevance.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Unsupervised Feature Relevance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"unsupervised feature relevance unsupervised feature relevance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Unsupervised Feature Relevance.md","fileName":"Unsupervised Feature Relevance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Unsupervised Feature Relevance","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 21:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Unsupervised Feature Selection for Clustering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Unsupervised Feature Selection for Clustering","dataclustering.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Unsupervised Feature Relevance.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Unsupervised Feature Relevance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"unsupervised feature relevance unsupervised feature relevance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Unsupervised Feature Relevance.md","fileName":"Unsupervised Feature Relevance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Unsupervised Feature Relevance","heading":"Unsupervised Feature Relevance","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A feature is relevant for unsupervised learning when it helps expose structure in the observations even though no class labels identify the desired groups. Relevance may mean preserving local neighborhoods, separating latent components, or supporting a compact and stable partition.\n\nThe difficulty is circular: clusters are used to judge features, while features determine the clusters that can be found. Practical methods therefore state an explicit structural criterion and compare candidate subsets or weights under that criterion.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Unsupervised Feature Selection for Clustering","dataclustering.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":